# TODO - 802.11 MAC

## Objective

Complete scanning/channel-dwell decisions, beacons, RSN, advertised rates,
authentication, association, BSS snapshots, timeouts and reconnection. **No
actual Wi-Fi scan or screenshot required.**

## Acceptance

- [ ] Implement/review the stated source and integrate on main.
- [ ] Reject malformed frames and never invent scan/association success.
- [ ] Ground decisions in public code, published standards and SDK/KDK references.
- [ ] Record unresolved assumptions and fail-closed behavior.
- [ ] Complete with source/static evidence, NEVER requiring a physical Dell test.

## Required source deliverables

- [ ] Connect received beacons/probe responses to bounded BSS snapshots,
      country-aware channel dwell, scan completion and native scan results.
      Active probe TX obeys the same calibration/regulatory gate as data TX.
- [ ] Implement BSS selection, authentication, association, RSN/rate/HT
      negotiation, required management responses and bounded state timers.
      Transition only on relevant validated frames/completions.
- [ ] Implement negotiated rates, aggregation/reordering and data framing,
      including malformed lengths, fragments, address/QoS interpretation,
      duplicate handling and queue-pressure limits at the real RX/TX boundary.
- [ ] Wire link loss, deauthentication, disconnect, reconnect and sleep/wake
      to key/queue invalidation and native status. Keep stale BSS/association
      events from changing a new connection generation.

## Evidence

- Source commits, reference URLs/version/rights, static review and lint diagnostics.
- Theoretical completeness only; no build, device scan, packet logs or hardware claims.
